  "label": "TMUA 2016 · Paper 1 · Question 5",
  "lead": "<img class=\"source-question\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Enlarge question\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"TMUA 2016 · Paper 1 · Question 5 — Find total unsigned area between x²-1 and the x-axis on [-2,2].\">",
  "options": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "C",
    "D",
    "E",
    "F"
  ],
  "correct": "C",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Find where the graph changes sign",
      "body": "<p>Sketch <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> between x=−2 and x=2. Solve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> and mark those points.</p>",
      "recap": "Split a geometric area where the graph meets the axis.",
      "pitfall": "A signed integral can cancel a piece below the axis.",
      "pause": "Mark which parts lie above and below the axis.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l21",
          "reminder": "Split a geometric area where the graph meets the axis."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Make every area contribution positive",
      "body": "<p>Integrate separately on the intervals you marked. Reverse the sign of any negative integral before adding the areas.</p>",
      "recap": "Geometric areas add, even when the signed integrals have opposite signs.",
      "pitfall": "If you use the graph’s symmetry, double the whole half-area, not just one piece.",
      "pause": "Evaluate each piece and add the positive areas.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l21",
          "reminder": "Geometric areas add, even when the signed integrals have opposite signs."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>The roots are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x000B1;</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>. The curve is below the axis for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> and above it on the two outer intervals. By even symmetry, the area is 2[<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" aria-label=\"integral from 0 to 1 of (1 minus x squared), with respect to x\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.18em\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>+<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" aria-label=\"integral from 1 to 2 of (x squared minus 1), with respect to x\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.18em\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>].</p><p>These integrals are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" aria-label=\"x minus x cubed over 3, evaluated from 0 to 1\"><msubsup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" aria-label=\"x cubed over 3 minus x, evaluated from 1 to 2\"><msubsup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>. The total is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>Answer C: 4.</strong></p>",
